            0.9,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "83"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.147,
            0.595,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "**Example 2 :** ABCD is a trapezium with AB || DC. E and F are points on non-parallel sides AD and BC respectively such that EF is parallel to AB"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.213,
            0.465,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": "(see Fig. 6.14). Show that $\\frac { \\mathrm { A E } } { \\mathrm { E D } }   =   \\frac { \\mathrm { B F } } { \\mathrm { F C } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.263,
            0.593,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Let us join AC to intersect EF at G (see Fig. 6.15)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.307,
            0.472,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": "AB || DC and EF || AB (Given)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.333,
            0.594,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\mathrm { E F } \\parallel \\mathrm { D C }$ (Lines parallel to the same line are parallel to each other)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.377,
            0.26,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": "Now, in $\\Delta   \\mathrm { A D C }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.402,
            0.409,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": "EG  \\parallel  DC  \\quad ( As EF  \\parallel  DC )",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.434,
            0.426,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": "So, ${ \\frac { \\mathrm { A E } } { \\mathrm { E D } } }   =   { \\frac { \\mathrm { A G } } { \\mathrm { G C } } }$ (Theorem 6.1)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.497,
            0.448,
            0.53,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "(1)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.484,
            0.324,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "Similarly, from $\\Delta \\mathrm { C A B }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.612,
            0.147,
            0.902,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.705,
                0.277,
                0.806,
                0.297
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 6.14"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.368,
            0.515,
            0.494,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{ CG }{ AG } \\equiv \\frac{ GF }{ BF }",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.375,
            0.574,
            0.495,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{AG}}{\\mathrm{GC}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{BF}}{\\mathrm{FC}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.592,
            0.359,
            0.901,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
