        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.588,
            0.14,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.625,
            0.371,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, from (1) and (2),"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.379,
            0.587,
            0.898,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { \\mathrm { A E } } { \\mathrm { E D } } } =   { \\frac { \\mathrm { B F } } { \\mathrm { F C } } }\\tag{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.715,
            0.594,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": "**Example 3 :** In Fig. 6.16, ${ \\frac { \\mathrm { P S } } { \\mathrm { S Q } } } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { P T } } { \\mathrm { T R } } }$ and $\\angle \\mathrm{PST} =$ $\\angle \\operatorname { P R Q } ,$ . Prove that PQR is an isosceles triangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.793,
            0.457,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** It is given that $\\frac { \\mathrm { P S } } { \\mathrm { S Q } }   =   \\frac { \\mathrm { P T } } { \\mathrm { T R } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.617,
            0.599,
            0.872,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.695,
